DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
The Municipal Manager shall be the Administrative Head of the Municipality and shall report to the Municipal Board and be responsible for the following functions:
Act on behalf of the Municipal Board ensuring the execution of the decisions of the board;
Prepare and present for approval to the Board of the Municipality, an annual estimate of revenue and expenditure;
Be principally responsible for building and maintaining a strong alliance and effective working relationships between the Board and the civil society, private sector, and community-based organizations;
Prepare, and submit to the Board an annual report on the activities and accomplishments of the departments and agencies comprising the executive branch of the board;
Act as an ex-officio member of all committees of the Board;
Exercise supervision over all departments and agencies of the Municipality and coordination of its activities;
Administer and enforce all Municipality By-laws, resolutions, franchises, leases, contracts, permits, and othe Municipality decisions;
Prepare and administer the annual Municipality budget;
Administer Municipality utilities and property;
Encourage and support regional and intergovernmental cooperation;
Promote cooperation among the Board of the Municipality, staff, and citizens in developing Municipality policies and building a sense of community, and
Perform any other duties as directed by the Board of the Municipality.
REQUIREMENTS FOR APPOINTMENT
Subject to Article 232 of the Constitution, a person shall qualify to be appointed as city or Municipal Manager if the Person; -
Is a citizen of Kenya
Holds a degree from a university recognized in Kenya or its equivalent;
Has proven experience of not less than five (5) years in administration or management either in the public or private sector; and
Be ordinarily a resident or have a permanent dwelling within the County.
Be holder of a Senior Management Course training from Kenya School of Government

Objective of the Consultancy:
The overall objective of the consultancy is to support the implementation of the Health & Safety (H&S) Support Service by:
Creating comprehensive, country-specific H&S Handbooks tailored to minigrid developers operating in Nigeria, Zambia, and Kenya;
Training and building the capacity of AMDA staff to support H&S compliance and awareness among members;
Developing and setting up a virtual Minigrid H&S Help Desk.
Scope of Work
The consultant's scope of work will encompass the following activities, aligned with the project's components:
H&S Country Handbooks
Develop three comprehensive handbooks (one each for Nigeria, Zambia, and Kenya), including:
Overview of country-specific H&S laws and regulatory frameworks;
Sector-specific risks and mitigation practices;
Compliance checklists and templates;
Case studies and success stories (where applicable);
Incorporate insights from the H&S protocol mapping exercise.
Ensure content is accessible, practical, and aligned with national licensing requirements for minigrids.
Collaborate with the AMDA Communications team for final formatting and design.
Capacity Building
Design and deliver training modules for AMDA staff on:
National and regional H&S regulations relevant to minigrids;
Best practices in incident reporting, compliance monitoring, and mitigation;
Use of the Minigrid Help Desk platform and resource materials;
Support AMDA staff in becoming H&S focal points within their regions.
Conduct virtual and/or in-person workshops and create a training manual or toolkit.
Development of the Minigrid H&S Help Desk
Design and structure the Help Desk interface and workflow (in collaboration with AMDA’s technical team).
Define standard operating procedures (SOPs) for handling inquiries, referrals, and incident reporting.
Create a database of certified H&S consultants for referrals.
Provide technical documentation and guidance for future updates and maintenance.
Consultant Qualifications
The ideal consultant will possess the following qualifications and experience:
Technical Expertise:
Minimum of 7 years of experience and demonstrated expertise in Health and Safety (H&S) regulations, protocols, and best practices, particularly within the energy or infrastructure sectors;
Experience with DRE solutions, minigrids, or off-grid energy technologies is highly desirable;
Knowledge of H&S regulatory landscapes in Sub-Saharan African countries, specifically Nigeria, Zambia, and Kenya, is a significant advantage

Job Summary:
The successful candidates will be reporting to the Dean School of Pharmacy and Health Sciences, the incumbent will be expected to teach, selected course in Human Anatomy including, Gross Anatomy, Embryology and Histology,
Key Responsibilities
Teach and assess selected Anatomy courses to undergraduate students in Bachelor of Science Nursing and Bachelor of Pharmacy
Introduce and mark practical reports for assigned courses that have practical component
Perform any other duties as may be assigned from time to time.
Support and mentor students in their career endeavors.
Participate in curriculum development activities to ensure that the programs and the teaching content are up-to-date and marketable;
Participate in program assessment and reviews;
Minimum Educational Qualifications and Professional Experience
A Master of science degree in Human Anatomy, Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of surgery, Bachelor of Pharmacy, Bachelor of Clinical Medicine, Bachelor of Nursing or any related discipline from recognized/accredited university.
A PhD in Human Anatomy from recognized/accredited university will be an added advantage.
Should have at least three (3) years of University teaching experience
Been registered by the relevant Professional Body
Personal Attributes & Competencies
Excellent computer background;
Be self-motivated and highly-disciplined;
Excellent command of the subject area including lesson planning;
Managing ambiguity and emotions;
Managing technological change;
Excellent communication skills;
Excellent listening and mediation skills;
Excellent fundraising and grants writing skills;
Excellent presentation skills;
Excellent research writing skills.

