WHO WE ARE LOOKING FOR
A highly motivated and organized individual with a strong background in data analysis and research;
Have a proven track record of collecting, cleaning, and analysing complex data to produce meaningful insights;
Have excellent communication and interpersonal skills, as they will be responsible for working with a variety of stakeholders, including AMDA members, donors, and government officials;
Have excellent Project Management skills. The candidate should have strong organizational skills to manage multiple research projects simultaneously, meet deadlines, and deliver high-quality work.
WHAT YOU WILL MAKE HAPPEN
Collect, clean, and analyze data on the minigrid sector in Africa. This includes gathering data from a variety of sources, such as government reports, industry surveys, and academic research. The Research Data Associate will also be responsible for cleaning and preparing the data for analysis;
Research minigrid-related topics. This could include topics such as the cost of minigrids, the impact of minigrids on economic development, and the challenges and opportunities facing the minigrid sector. The Research Data Associate will use their analytical skills to produce meaningful insights from the data;
Prepare reports, presentations, and other materials that use data to tell the story of the minigrid sector. The Research Data Associate will be responsible for communicating their research findings to a variety of audiences, including AMDA members, donors, government officials, and the media. They will need to be able to communicate complex data clearly and concisely;
Work with AMDA members, donors, and government officials to share data and insights. The Research Data Associate will play a key role in building relationships with stakeholders and sharing AMDA's research findings. They will also be responsible for providing technical support to stakeholders on data-related issues;
Develop and maintain AMDA's data infrastructure. This includes developing and implementing data collection and management systems, as well as developing data visualization tools.
WHAT YOU ALREADY HAVE
Bachelor's degree in statistics, data science, economics, or a related field;
5+ years of experience in data analysis and research;
Experience with statistical software, such as R or Python;
Experience with data visualization tools, such as Tableau or Power BI;
Strong understanding of research methodology;
Ability to create actionable insights from raw data;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
Ability to work independently and as part of a team.
WHAT WOULD GIVE YOU AN ADDED ADVANTAGE
Bi- or multi-lingual proficiency (French, Portuguese);
Basic knowledge in the renewable energy sector .
go to method of application »

Advert Ref: No. KWS/08/2025
Reporting to the Director General, the overall responsibility will be to ensure effective and efficient management of corporate affairs and compliance with enabling legal matters and other relevant legislations.
Duties & Responsibilities
Provide strategic leadership in the development of policies and regulations that guide in the management of the Service;
Spearhead the formulation, implementation and review of the Service’s legal strategies, guidelines and relevant regulations that contributes into the attainment of the Service’s mandate;
