Job Purpose
This position is established under Section 10 of the Kenya School of Government Act, 2012. The Director shall be responsible to the Director General for provision of strategic direction and leadership in the development and implementation of quality programs in training, research, consultancy and advisory services in order to realize the mandate of the School; ensuring effective and efficient use of resources; and building visibility and presence of the School in the Region.
Job Descriptions
Duties and responsibilities at this level will entail:
Overseeing provision of training, research, consultancy and advisory services at the School;
Overseeing implementation of approved curricula at the Campus;
Coordinating preparation of quarterly and annual reports on training, research and consultancy activities at the Campus;
Overseeing implementation of quality management systems in the campus
Coordinating promotion of a corporate culture to strategically position the School through branding and visibility activities;
Managing implementation of service delivery standards and charters to raise the customer satisfaction index;
Ensuring proper financial management and prudent utilization of the School’s resources and assets;
Facilitating staff development and performance management;
Overseeing development, implementation and review of performance and Quality Management Systems in the Campus;
Overseeing preparation of campus and employee work plans, setting and evaluation of performance targets and contracts for the Campus; and
Overseeing preparation, implementation and review of annual budgets and procurement plans for the Campus.
Job Specifications
For appointment to this grade, an officer must have: -
Bachelor’s Degree from a recognized university in a relevant field;
Master’s Degree from a recognized university in a relevant field;
Fifteen (15) years relevant cumulative experience, three (3) being in senior management position in an institution of higher learning or any other relevant Institution;
Membership to a relevant professional body or association;
