Job Description:
The Communications Coordinator works closely with the Executive Director and the Sustain Africa team, supporting strategic communications that advance Sustain Africa’s mission and engagement with stakeholders, partners, and the broader audience. This role leads content development, media relations, digital engagement, and storytelling, ensuring Sustain Africa’s messaging remains clear, impactful, and aligned with its objectives and IFDCs communications strategy. In addition to communications leadership, the Communications Coordinator provides operational support across Sustain Africa’s broader program activities, assisting with cross-functional coordination, stakeholder engagement, and logistical execution to enhance program implementation.
Responsibilities:
Strategic Communications
Develop and implement a communications strategy aligned with Sustain Africa’s objectives and IFDC’s regional communications strategy;
Ensure consistent branding, messaging, tone, and visual identity across all channels;
Provide strategic guidance on reputational matters and messaging.
Communications Outputs and Storytelling
Create diverse written content, including blog posts, press releases, newsletters, and opinion pieces;
Support visual content development through graphic design;
Liaise with contractors for content production and visibility materials;
Coordinate internal communications and Sustain Africa events, campaigns, and launches.
Media Engagement
Build and maintain relationships with media outlets and journalists, supporting media visits and interviews;
Draft and distribute press releases and promotional materials to maximize coverage;
Handle media inquiries in coordination with internal teams.
Social Media & Digital Engagement
Manage digital engagement across platforms (Facebook, LinkedIn, X, Instagram);
Oversee Sustain Africa’s website, including content creation, optimization, and updates;
Track performance metrics and refined digital strategies.
Projects, Processes & Reporting
Develop and implement efficient communications processes and procedures;
Support copywriting, proofreading, and translation of donor reports and fact sheets;
Select and implement tools that enhance Sustain Africa’s communications efficiency;
Manage digital assets, ensuring ethical communication practices;
Monitor and report on communications impact and audience engagement.
Operations
Oversee logistics, resource allocation, and execution of communications activities;
Support procurement of materials and services related to media, events, and visibility;
Collaborate across departments to ensure seamless execution of strategic initiatives;
Manage communications budgets, balancing cost-effectiveness and quality;
Provide operational support beyond communications, contributing to broader Sustain Africa program operations as needed;
Travel within the region and potentially beyond, supporting Sustain Africa’s initiatives, stakeholder engagement, and program implementation across multiple countries.
Requirements
A Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Journalism, Public Affairs, Knowledge Management, or a related field;
Minimum of three to five years in communications, public relations, or media, preferably within development, donor, or impact-driven organizations;
Proven ability to manage multi-channel communication campaigns, translating complex or technical content into compelling narratives for diverse audiences;
Hands-on expertise in digital platform management (social media, CMS websites), with a strong focus on user engagement;
Experience collaborating across different cultural contexts and working with international partners;
Exceptional writing and editing abilities, delivering high-quality content under tight deadlines;
Strong interpersonal and presentation skills, fostering relationships across internal teams and external stakeholders;
Analytical and strategic thinking, ensuring key messages are communicated effectively;
Proficiency in digital tools and design software (e.g., Canva, Adobe Creative Suite), with experience in analytics platforms;
Ability to manage multiple tasks independently, ensuring timely execution of projects.

Job Description
Duties and responsibilities at this level will entail:-
Coordinating the development, implementation and review of administration policies, strategies, regulations, guidelines, standards and procedures;
Coordinating fleet management;
Planning and coordinating office accommodation;
Overseeing repairs and maintenance schedules and logs for institute’s vehicles, office furniture, office premises;
Ensuring renewal of general insurance covers for vehicles, buildings and equipment;
Coordinating the development and maintenance of tools and equipment register;
Ensuring provision of office equipment, furniture and facilities;
Coordinating identification of obsolete assets and manage the disposal process;
Managing telephone, registry and security services;
Coordinating outsourced services;
Ensuring Authority’s adherence to employees’ safety health and welfare in accordance to Occupational Safety and Health Act, 2007;
Coordinating development and maintenance of security systems for the Institute;
Coordinating and managing bills, land rates and utilities;
Safeguarding the Institute’s assets including office premises, vehicle, office equipment and furniture; and
Ensuring the maintenance of up-to-date inventories of the institute’s establishment, equipment and facilities.
Requirements for Appointment
For appointment to this grade, a candidate must have:-
Cumulative service period of twelve (12) years’ work experience, three (3) of which should have been at the level of Principal Administration Officer II or in a comparable position;
Bachelor’s Degree in any of the following disciplines: - Public Administration, Business Administration, Transport and Logistics or its equivalent qualification from a recognized Institution;i
Master’s Degree in any of the following disciplines: - Human Resource Development, Business Administration, Transport and Logistics or its equivalent qualification from a recognized Institution.)
Management course lasting not less than four (4) weeks from a recognized institution;
Membership to a professional body in good standing where applicable;
Proficiency in computer applications; and
Demonstrated a high degree of professional competence and administrative capability as reflected in work performance and results.
